      "heading": "About the work from home job/internship",
      "html": "<p>As an HR intern at NayePankh Foundation, you will have the opportunity to immerse yourself in the world of non-profit organizations while gaining hands-on experience in human resources. You will work closely with our HR team to support various initiatives and projects aimed at recruiting, developing, and retaining top talent for our organization. <br>
<br>
Selected intern's day-to-day responsibilities include:<br>
<br>
1. Assist with recruitment efforts by posting job listings, screening resumes, and scheduling interviews.<br>
2. Help onboard new employees by preparing paperwork, coordinating orientation sessions, and ensuring a smooth integration into the company.<br>
3. Support training and development programs by organizing training sessions, tracking employee progress, and collecting feedback.<br>
4. Assist with performance management processes by maintaining employee records, conducting performance evaluations, and addressing any performance-related issues.<br>
5. Contribute to employee engagement initiatives by organizing team-building activities, gathering employee feedback, and implementing programs to enhance the overall employee experience.<br>
6. Assist with benefits administration by enrolling employees in benefit programs, answering benefits-related questions, and ensuring compliance with regulations.<br>
7. Support the HR team with various administrative tasks, such as maintaining HR databases, preparing reports, and ensuring accurate record-keeping. <br>
